{"kind":"report","text":"Critical security Source triage delivered for request b79cc294, original witness head c8dbeaa20140ab7215f64e3f4b71e5068ea71c10/tree 5eba62c87387069f2e181b9bc79ba674c7bb813c. The two witness bodies were read first and completely by checker Root and both independent reviewers. Production differs from receiving main2a40 only by those two test files. Both sealed reviewer reports were read completely; my own complete application factory and selected validator, namespace, handler, destination and directory units corroborate the principal boundaries. This report accepts no repair and performs no attack.\n\nThe durable owner checkpoint3542ef54 reports run93494: compiler0, one native case1, postguard passed, stopping when A-to-B opened a publication. The test throws that critical message only after finding a newly opened publication in the native destination summary. Its grants, membership, rules, scopes and factory are real; Git host and clock are labelled stand-ins. The same-room branch, attack judgment and push were not run. Original scope IDs/history were not captured by the reporter, and have not been invented, reconstructed or recovered by a rerun. Owner execution remains owner evidence; checker inspected no private result or log.\n\nThe source trust boundary is missing: an ordinary capability-free application can declare name change, receive an arbitrary destination as domain data, and be created as kind lane. Its authentic source entry is exported under that chosen name. Handler selection matches lane/change, while reserve checks that the operation belongs to its sender, duplicates and receipt capacity; it does not establish a trusted publication lane in the destination's room. Source authenticity and self-owned operation are not destination publication permission.\n\nRepair constraints: creator equality alone includes same-room applications. Directory lane-row presence or kind=pr also is not creation proof: index accepts any lane's advisory with no guards, and index-row creates an unseen sender's row using supplied fields. Verify actual trusted native creation cause/entry/seed and accepted child correspondence, eligible declaration, full scope/incarnation and destination-room relationship. A bare chosen name or digest does not establish this. An authenticated native open-pr registration can differ from application establishment; preserve the legitimate lane versions, declarations, extensions and normal app workflows rather than banning every digest-pinned native change/issue declaration indiscriminately.\n\nCover existing stored declarations, fresh/reloaded pins, cached sender paths and queued work. A new-activation-only name rule is insufficient evidence for these paths; do not assume an old cache survives a deployment either. Preserve historical bytes, hashes, signatures, custody and uncertain operations, and state how unsupported old declarations and already queued privilege transitions are fenced without rewriting their past outcomes. The repair must protect existing state, not merely reject a fresh fixture.\n\nApply verified eligibility consistently to reserve and withdraw. An advisory-forged row must not acquire authority. Review analogous change-name consumers, including issue.closes; that path has not been fully traced or attacked, so no separate issue exploit is claimed. Existing publication binding limits withdraw cancellation, and later destination judgment retains native authority/policy checks; publication opening is not proof of a pushed commit. Keep separately authorized fold publication distinct from legacy reserve privilege.\n\nIndependent repair review needs explicit native refusal evidence for cross-room and same-room applications, preexisting/queued cases, advisory-created rows and wrong incarnations, plus positive legitimate native publication and compatibility coverage. Preserve the original failed observation and unrun branch; run any new regression under its own changed-head provenance and one appropriate gate. No provider deployment or historical witness reproduction is authorized by this report. The complete fix remains owed under original2ce; CLI landing and Lending review remain held by the critical priority.\n\nArchitecture: make eligibility a verified relationship independent of a chosen family name. Security: authenticate both the source and its privilege to affect this destination. Simplification: share the eligibility rule across privileged legacy paths while preserving native and fold contracts. Coverage outside the named complete bodies/units remains partial; no peer body credit is borrowed. No Source edits, execution, private proof, credentials, browser, provider or network operations by checker."}